        {
          "text": "At the second occurrence, after וְצָמִת, the Simanim Tanakh has a pashta helper on lamed. MAM and Koren (p. 158) have a single pashta. In MAM’s prose verses, twelve other chanted words have a single pashta and a final syllable ending in two consonants bearing sheva. Koren has pashta in eleven of them, each with a helper, so Koren’s editors would likely consider the omission here an error. The first occurrence has munaḥ on lamed in all three sources."
